<title>TURKEY: Turk Koc Hldg '96 net profits up 80 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Koc Hldg '96 net profits up 80 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 final results</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	667.69   vs     617.07</p>
<p>    Net profit		     6,676.86   vs   3,702.43</p>
<p>    Operating loss		   581.89   vs     334.37</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	   8,573.91   vs   4,895.35</p>
<p>    Interest Paid		     0	 vs	 0</p>
<p>    Total debts		    1,716.29   vs   1,077.52</p>
<p>    Equity			  23,947.84   vs  14,124.36</p>
<p>    Capital			 10,000.00   vs   6,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Koc Holding A.S. is the parent company of Turkey's leading industrial conglomerate.</p>
<p>The company plans to pay a 150 lira cash dividend per 1,000 lira nominal valued share from its 1996 profits after approval at the annual meeting of shareholders and directors.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 84.9 percent wholesale inflation in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875 GUZ EKS</p>
